.SS "static \fBvoid\fP Assimp::SceneCombiner::MergeMaterials (\fBaiMaterial\fP ** dest, std::vector< \fBaiMaterial\fP * >::const_iterator begin, std::vector< \fBaiMaterial\fP * >::const_iterator end)\fR [static]\fP"
Merges two or more materials
.PP
The materials should be complementary as much as possible\&. In case of a property present in different materials, the first occurrence is used\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdest\fP Destination material\&. Must be empty\&. 
.br
\fIbegin\fP First material to be processed 
.br
\fIend\fP Points to the material after the last material to be processed 
.RE
.PP

.SS "static \fBvoid\fP Assimp::SceneCombiner::MergeMeshes (\fBaiMesh\fP ** dest, unsigned int flags, std::vector< \fBaiMesh\fP * >::const_iterator begin, std::vector< \fBaiMesh\fP * >::const_iterator end)\fR [static]\fP"
Merges two or more meshes
.PP
The meshes should have equal vertex formats\&. Only components that are provided by ALL meshes will be present in the output mesh\&. An exception is made for VColors - they are set to black\&. The meshes should have the same material indices, too\&. The output material index is always the material index of the first mesh\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdest\fP Destination mesh\&. Must be empty\&. 
.br
\fIflags\fP Currently no parameters 
.br
\fIbegin\fP First mesh to be processed 
.br
\fIend\fP Points to the mesh after the last mesh to be processed 
.RE
.PP

.SS "static \fBvoid\fP Assimp::SceneCombiner::MergeScenes (\fBaiScene\fP ** dest, \fBaiScene\fP * master, std::vector< \fBAttachmentInfo\fP > & src, unsigned int flags = \fR0\fP)\fR [static]\fP"
Merges two or more scenes and attaches all scenes to a specific position in the node graph of the master scene\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdest\fP Receives a pointer to the destination scene\&. If the pointer doesn't point to nullptr when the function is called, the existing scene is cleared and refilled\&. 
.br
\fImaster\fP Master scene\&. It will be deleted afterwards\&. All other scenes will be inserted in its node graph\&. 
.br
\fIsrc\fP Non-empty list of scenes to be merged along with their corresponding attachment points in the master scene\&. The function deletes the input scenes afterwards\&. There may be duplicate scenes\&. 
.br
\fIflags\fP Combination of the AI_INT_MERGE_SCENE flags defined above 
.RE
.PP

.SS "static \fBvoid\fP Assimp::SceneCombiner::MergeScenes (\fBaiScene\fP ** dest, std::vector< \fBaiScene\fP * > & src, unsigned int flags = \fR0\fP)\fR [static]\fP"
Merges two or more scenes\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdest\fP Receives a pointer to the destination scene\&. If the pointer doesn't point to nullptr when the function is called, the existing scene is cleared and refilled\&. 
.br
